# L §8.4 (tally 2.3, #247; the review of G3, Q7): a row's `window(a, b)` with a after b is `LOAD-DOMAIN`
# naming the written days, as the engine prints. Before: the literal `window(a, b)`.
=== m.tally
model b
  tally 2
  on 2026-08-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ix = [k1, k2]
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input pay: money PLN
input d1: date
input d2: date
input x: date
input ds: dates
input n: int
input hol: calendar
input lot: (bought date, cnt int)
input rate[d in days]: num
band tax(v: num): num
def g: date
  rule base = d1
  rule other = d2 when d1 == d2
def h: date = d1
def hl: date = d1 at d1
move salary: transfers
  on d1
  at d1
  when d1 == d1
  leg cash from world to konto amount pay
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  pay = 1 000.00 PLN "c"
  d1 = 2026-04-06 "c"
  d2 = 2026-04-13 "c"
  x = window(2026-04-13, 2026-04-10) "c"
  ds = [2026-04-06, 2026-04-13] "c"
  n = 3 "c"
  hol = calendar(weekends [sat, sun], yearly [01-01], added [2026-04-06]) "c"
  lot = (bought: 2026-04-06, cnt: 3) "c"
  rate[*] = 2 "c"
  tax: [0, inf) = 1 "c"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-DOMAIN window(2026-04-13, 2026-04-10) with a after b (L §8.4) (m.tally:38)
